                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.62/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wallace</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-13T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1920, noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            January 14, 2.32 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>123. Department’s 8 January 2, 6 p.m. Dresel will leave here Wednesday evening
                    [January] 14 with Dulles and three clerks. Dolbeare and Foster are proceeding
                    direct from Rotterdam. Dresel and Dulles will stop over in Coblenz and reach
                    Berlin Saturday morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
